From 55da2041ae15f75b02c20dad4b8a251aac68e703 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Victor C." <34163765+vicajilau@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 06:51:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 01/23] core: Implement per-monitor workspaces support

Add the initial infrastructure for per-monitor workspaces, where each
logical monitor keeps its own workspace list and its own active
workspace, rather than the display having a single global one.

Key changes:
- Add a GSetting for per-monitor workspaces.
- Maintain a workspace list and an active workspace per logical monitor.
- Assign newly placed and moved windows to the active workspace of the
  monitor they are on.
- Update window visibility and monitor hotplug handling for the new mode.
- Keep the classic global workspace mode unchanged when the feature is
  disabled.

The mode is limited to static workspaces for now. With dynamic
workspaces the workspace set is expected to be actively managed by the
shell, which has no per-monitor counterpart yet.

Based on initial work by Chris Willingham.

Part-of: <https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/mutter/-/issues/37>
