Subject: [PATCH 03/23] workspace-manager: Notify n-workspaces after building
 per-monitor workspaces

meta_workspace_manager_setup_per_monitor_workspaces() drops the workspaces
created during init and builds a new list with meta_workspace_new(), which
neither emits 'workspace-added'/'workspace-removed' nor notifies the
'n-workspaces' property. The workspace set therefore changed without anything
outside the workspace manager being told.

gnome-shell rebuilds its workspace views, its thumbnails box and its panel
indicators on 'notify::n-workspaces', so all of them kept the state they had
before the per-monitor workspaces existed, which is why the panel showed a
single workspace dot regardless of the configured workspace count.

Notify the property once the new list is in place.
