From 47786785b522d9e3bc898f0fad75297922187bc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Victor C." <34163765+vicajilau@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 19:04:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 06/23] workspace: Give workspaces a container instead of a
 cached index

MetaMonitorWorkspaceState held the workspace list and the active
workspace of one monitor, and each workspace cached its position in that
list in a monitor_index field, maintained by hand in five places.
meta_workspace_index() meanwhile indexed into the manager's global list,
which does not describe a workspace's position in per-monitor mode.

Rename the struct to MetaWorkspaceContainer, which is what it is: either
the global set of workspaces or one set per logical monitor, each with
its own active workspace. Give MetaWorkspace a pointer to the container
it belongs to, and derive the index from that instead of caching it.

That removes the parallel bookkeeping and lets three places stop
searching for the container a workspace belongs to:

- meta_workspace_manager_remove_from_container(), which walked every
  container looking for the workspace.
- meta_workspace_activate_with_focus(), which walked every container and
  then mapped a monitor number back to a MetaLogicalMonitor.
- The renumbering loop that ran after every removal.

Also set the container's monitor when it is created. It was only ever
assigned when re-keying on a monitor change, so the matching there had
to reach through the first workspace of the container to find out which
monitor it belonged to.
