The switch-to-workspace keybindings resolved their target against global
state: the numbered ones indexed into the manager's workspace list, and
the directional ones started from the global active workspace.

With per-monitor workspaces that list holds the workspaces of every
monitor one after another, and the global active workspace is the first
workspace of the first monitor, so the shortcuts only ever drove the
first monitor no matter which one was being used.

Resolve them against the workspaces of the monitor the pointer is on
instead. meta_workspace_get_neighbor() already picks neighbours within a
monitor's list, so the directional ones only needed the right starting
workspace.
