From 598be0055d74921e7e270badea0f573c102abdc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Victor C." <34163765+vicajilau@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 08:19:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/23] display: Rebuild the workspace containers before the
 windows react

The per-monitor containers were rebuilt from a handler for the monitor
manager's monitors-changed, which is emitted after monitors-changed-internal,
and it is on the internal one that MetaDisplay fixes up the monitor of every
window.

Windows therefore reacted to the new monitors while the containers still
described the old ones. Asking for the workspaces of the monitor a window
had just landed on found nothing, so a window whose monitor went away was
not moved to a workspace of the monitor it ended up on, and stayed on a
workspace of a monitor that no longer exists.

Rebuild them from MetaDisplay's own handler instead, before anything looks
at the new monitors. Connecting the workspace manager to the internal signal
would not do, since it is created after the display connects to it, so its
handler would still run second.
---
