From 3fe77948b6d39ae726abb7db1dea427fdc23d1f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Victor C." <34163765+vicajilau@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 07:57:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/23] x11: Identify workspaces globally in the EWMH and
 workarea properties

_NET_WM_DESKTOP, _NET_CURRENT_DESKTOP and _GTK_WORKAREAS_D%d are a single
flat numbering of every workspace, shared with every X11 client, and
_NET_NUMBER_OF_DESKTOPS counts all of them. There is no monitor in that
protocol to tell two workspaces with the same monitor-relative position
apart, so these have to use the global index.

The same applies to the workspace recorded in a toplevel's session state,
which is restored with meta_window_change_workspace_by_index() against the
global list.
---
