From c4984512d81f85bb71f922f1bae1e3bf377fe772 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Victor C." <34163765+vicajilau@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 07:57:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/23] workspace-manager: Identify workspaces globally outside
 the containers

The workspace manager hands out numbers that index its own list of every
workspace, so those have to be global:

 - workspace-added carries the position in that list, which is what the
   handlers look the new workspace up with
 - meta_workspace_manager_get_active_workspace_index() is the inverse of
   meta_workspace_manager_get_workspace_by_index()
 - removing a workspace compares the removed position against the active
   one from that same API, so both have to count the same workspaces

meta_workspace_manager_reorder_workspace() was reordering the global list
after finding the workspace in it, but took the position to move from the
monitor-relative index. With per-monitor workspaces that moved the wrong
workspace, or refused to move one that was already at that position on its
own monitor.

The two monitor-relative uses left are debug messages that name a monitor,
where the position within that monitor is what is meaningful.
---
