MetaPluginClass::switch_workspace is given the workspaces to animate
between as positions in the global list, so the plugins have to compare
against the same list when deciding which actors belong to the outgoing and
incoming workspace. With per-monitor workspaces they were comparing a
monitor-relative position against those numbers, so windows ended up parented
