From 959c1a76c06c3a263df68bcdecb2b7ad26b2a891 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Victor C." <34163765+vicajilau@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 08:01:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 23/23] workspace: Drop meta_workspace_index()

Every caller now asks for the index it meant. What is left is a function
whose answer depends on a setting the caller did not look at, and whose
name gives no hint that there is a choice to make, which is how the bugs
fixed in the previous commits got in.

This drops a public function without a replacement of the same name, so
consumers have to pick between meta_workspace_get_global_index() and
meta_workspace_get_index_on_monitor(). That is the point: there is no
answer that is right for both, and the compiler saying so is better than
every caller silently getting the one that suits the current setting.
